        "results_interpretation": "The pooled results from ten studies indicate that zinc is not associated with breast cancer survival, as the effect size of 0.86 (95% CI: 0.71, 1.04) is not statistically significant, given that the confidence interval includes the null value of 1. Additionally, the high heterogeneity (I\u00b2 = 88.0%) suggests substantial variability among the studies, which may affect the reliability of the pooled effect size. Thus, further investigation is needed to clarify the relationship between zinc and breast cancer survival."
